{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And they will listen to your voice</b> — from them: once you say this language to them, they will immediately listen to your voice, for this sign is already handed down among them from Jacob and from Joseph, that with this language they will be redeemed. Jacob said to them: \"And Elohim will surely visit you\" (Genesis 50:24); Joseph said to them: \"Elohim will surely visit you\" (ibid. v. 25). This is the language of Rashi. (Rashi on Exodus 3:18) Perhaps the Rav will expound that Joseph said twice פקד יפקד, to signify that a tradition was in his hand from his father. And in Shemot Rabbah (3:8): immediately <b>and they will listen to your voice</b> — why? Because a tradition of redemption is in their hand, so that any redeemer who comes and says to them a doubled פקידה, he is a true redeemer — this is their language in that aggadah. And one must ask: from where would they know to believe him? Perhaps Moses heard this tradition just as they did. And the answer is that they received it from Joseph, who heard it from the mouth of their father the prophet — that the first one to come and say to them in this language, he will be their redeemer. It is revealed and known before HaKadosh Barukh Hu that no man would come and falsify it to them; in this He assured them. But in another place I found there (Shemot Rabbah 5:1): Rabbi Ḥama bar Rabbi Ḥanina said — Moses was taken from his father's house at the age of twelve. Why? Because had he grown up in his father's house and come and told them these matters, they would not have believed him, for they would say: his father transmitted them to him. For Joseph transmitted it to Levi, and Levi to Kehat, and Kehat to Amram. Therefore he was taken from his father's house, and when he went and told Israel all these things, therefore they believed him, as it is stated (Exodus 4:31): \"And the people believed.\" And their intent in saying \"Joseph transmitted it to Levi\" is to say that Jacob revealed his secret to Joseph out of his love for him; with that very language Joseph made all his brothers swear, and revealed it to Levi because he — Levi — said it to them in that language on account of the tradition in his hand from his father, and commanded that the matter remain a secret."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The citation '(בשמו\"ר ה א)' refers to Shemot Rabbah 5:1, resolved by matching the named sage and content."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:02:04.367139025Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}